WEBVTT

00:01.016 --> 00:12.702
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, by 2 p.m., Paul Ribeiro has returned to the Palace of Jeon, going through the different fortifications and into the royal chambers.

00:16.523 --> 00:17.584
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you want to do?

00:17.604 --> 00:21.806
[SPEAKER_01]: You gotta look for Jeon.

00:22.386 --> 00:24.587
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so you want to go up to his private offices?

00:25.127 --> 00:25.327
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

00:25.928 --> 00:26.268
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

00:30.058 --> 00:35.119
[SPEAKER_01]: You get there, it's around 2 p.m., and his guards are outside in front as normal.

00:36.420 --> 00:38.040
[SPEAKER_01]: And you go up to them and what do you say?

00:38.660 --> 00:40.961
[SPEAKER_01]: I need to speak to Prince Jeon, please.

00:43.921 --> 00:44.361
[SPEAKER_01]: Can I ask?

00:44.681 --> 00:46.122
[SPEAKER_01]: Can I tell him what this is about?

00:48.322 --> 00:48.842
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm Paul.

00:50.323 --> 00:50.803
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Paul.

00:50.823 --> 00:51.503
[SPEAKER_01]: He's very busy.

00:51.523 --> 00:51.963
[SPEAKER_01]: What is it?

00:53.223 --> 00:54.164
[SPEAKER_00]: It's important matters.

00:57.644 --> 00:58.165
[SPEAKER_00]: Regarding?

00:59.005 --> 00:59.645
[SPEAKER_00]: Not your concern.

01:01.485 --> 01:01.765
[SPEAKER_01]: I see.

01:03.387 --> 01:04.408
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll see if he will see you.

01:06.830 --> 01:09.212
[SPEAKER_01]: He walks into the chamber.

01:13.155 --> 01:19.501
[SPEAKER_01]: Normally, John would have scheduled a time with you.

01:20.162 --> 01:23.465
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, he was attentive, but obviously very, very

01:29.806 --> 01:34.007
[SPEAKER_01]: He was concerned about making sure things were done in a way.

01:34.027 --> 01:36.507
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't want to give you access to them all the time, right?

01:37.428 --> 01:45.849
[SPEAKER_01]: But the guard does come back out and he says, he'll see you, opens the door, and Jeon is behind the desk.

01:47.370 --> 01:51.490
[SPEAKER_01]: You walk in, and the guard closes the door behind you.

01:53.191 --> 01:54.051
[SPEAKER_01]: Jeon says to you,

01:56.539 --> 01:57.760
[SPEAKER_01]: Paul, this better be important.

01:57.820 --> 01:58.581
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm very busy.

01:59.481 --> 02:00.922
[SPEAKER_01]: We're dealing with a blockade now.

02:02.384 --> 02:02.884
[SPEAKER_00]: So I've heard.

02:02.904 --> 02:11.871
[SPEAKER_00]: I have learned a very great important news regarding me and my mother and my father.

02:14.613 --> 02:15.554
[SPEAKER_01]: That was quick.

02:16.415 --> 02:16.575
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

02:18.883 --> 02:32.852
[SPEAKER_00]: I found these letters that were written to my mother by a man of name Grayson, which I believe is my father, and is the son of Miss Jamis.

02:35.153 --> 02:35.974
[SPEAKER_00]: Lady Jamis?

02:36.174 --> 02:36.394
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

02:39.115 --> 02:40.336
[SPEAKER_00]: I have spoken with her already.

02:40.536 --> 02:42.778
[SPEAKER_01]: The son of Lady Jamis, but not Lord Jamis?

02:43.878 --> 02:45.679
[SPEAKER_00]: No, Lord Jamis.

02:45.900 --> 02:47.861
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah, Lord Jamis isn't Lady Jamis' son.

02:49.415 --> 02:50.955
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I knew Grace and his boy.

02:53.616 --> 02:55.476
[SPEAKER_00]: These letters confirm that he is my father.

02:59.497 --> 03:00.417
[SPEAKER_00]: Where did you find these?

03:01.018 --> 03:04.418
[SPEAKER_00]: I found them in my mother's room in a chest, hidden away.

03:04.618 --> 03:06.399
[SPEAKER_01]: I had searched her room many times.

03:06.719 --> 03:07.459
[SPEAKER_01]: Where was it hidden?

03:08.939 --> 03:13.120
[SPEAKER_00]: There was a closet.

03:13.140 --> 03:14.260
[SPEAKER_01]: The old chambers?

03:14.721 --> 03:14.901
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

03:15.121 --> 03:16.081
[SPEAKER_01]: The old secrets?

03:16.641 --> 03:16.821
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

03:28.893 --> 03:29.313
[SPEAKER_01]: Who's they?

03:31.054 --> 03:31.634
[SPEAKER_01]: Your mother.

03:32.974 --> 03:33.475
[SPEAKER_01]: Grayson.

03:34.315 --> 03:34.895
[SPEAKER_01]: Someone else.

03:35.435 --> 03:36.756
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously they had found it.

03:38.736 --> 03:40.557
[SPEAKER_01]: I knew she wanted that room for a reason.

03:42.698 --> 03:44.378
[SPEAKER_01]: She was very tricky in her ways.

03:46.539 --> 03:47.739
[SPEAKER_01]: You're sure it's Grayson here?

03:48.179 --> 03:49.080
[SPEAKER_01]: These letters prove it?

03:49.720 --> 03:50.020
[SPEAKER_01]: Read them.

03:51.601 --> 03:53.121
[SPEAKER_01]: He starts going through it.

03:58.043 --> 03:58.723
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically,

04:01.465 --> 04:11.850
[SPEAKER_01]: He has a scowl on his face at the beginning, but as he reads through the letters, you can tell that he is relieved.

04:17.573 --> 04:26.597
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually, he starts nodding and looking at these things.

04:32.535 --> 04:42.463
[SPEAKER_01]: And says to you, Well, Paul, I must say, you brought great peace to my mind.

04:43.703 --> 04:44.204
[SPEAKER_01]: I thought I would.

04:45.925 --> 04:49.428
[SPEAKER_01]: The scandal back 23 years ago was hard enough.

04:52.430 --> 04:55.813
[SPEAKER_01]: But honestly, Grayson Jamis is

05:01.391 --> 05:06.392
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I can accept him as your father much more than I can others.

05:08.032 --> 05:09.093
[SPEAKER_01]: Jason was a good man.

05:10.833 --> 05:23.095
[SPEAKER_01]: He was honorable and intelligent and I'm glad to know that he loved your mother.

05:25.696 --> 05:30.637
[SPEAKER_01]: They were inseparable as children and I think your mother had a great fondness for him and I'm glad to know that

05:36.258 --> 05:37.919
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm glad to know that he is your father.

05:38.860 --> 05:43.083
[SPEAKER_01]: Below your station, or my station as it were, your mother's station.

05:44.184 --> 05:48.067
[SPEAKER_01]: But things could have been much worse.

05:52.130 --> 05:52.530
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you mean?

06:01.637 --> 06:03.678
[SPEAKER_01]: The letters mention this man, Archibald.

06:04.099 --> 06:05.360
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I know of him.

06:09.040 --> 06:10.921
[SPEAKER_01]: He was a demon, Paul.

06:12.822 --> 06:17.845
[SPEAKER_01]: And the thought of you coming from him was unbearable to me.

06:21.467 --> 06:22.268
[SPEAKER_01]: He was cruel.

06:25.610 --> 06:28.431
[SPEAKER_01]: He was arrogant.

06:30.072 --> 06:34.055
[SPEAKER_01]: He thought himself above all stations, even though he had no name.

06:36.156 --> 06:37.697
[SPEAKER_00]: The worst part about him, however,

06:38.942 --> 06:43.423
[SPEAKER_01]: Was that he was brilliant.

06:46.103 --> 06:48.724
[SPEAKER_01]: His mind was like no others.

06:49.684 --> 06:54.865
[SPEAKER_01]: And his charm, although it was false, was incredible.

06:57.846 --> 07:01.587
[SPEAKER_01]: I learned at a very young age what Archibald truly was.

07:02.647 --> 07:08.488
[SPEAKER_01]: Because as he would charm those that were above him and manipulate them to his will,

07:09.593 --> 07:13.895
[SPEAKER_01]: Those that were weaker than him, he would torture.

07:14.976 --> 07:20.879
[SPEAKER_01]: And he knew how to do it in such a way that it would never come back to him.

07:22.300 --> 07:24.001
[SPEAKER_01]: His torture, you see, was not physical.

07:26.223 --> 07:26.943
[SPEAKER_01]: Not always.

07:27.123 --> 07:29.604
[SPEAKER_01]: Even though if he thought he could get away with that, he would.

07:31.005 --> 07:31.666
[SPEAKER_01]: It was mental.

07:32.066 --> 07:39.130
[SPEAKER_01]: And the mental anguish that he caused me, even though I was older than him,

07:40.660 --> 07:42.140
[SPEAKER_01]: Was not insignificant.

07:50.642 --> 08:04.105
[SPEAKER_01]: I always told my father that he was not a good influence on your mother and still he brought

08:06.105 --> 08:13.169
[SPEAKER_01]: Your mother, Grayson, and other couriers in our land into his orbit to do what he did.

08:13.830 --> 08:16.511
[SPEAKER_01]: I could see through him though, and I knew what he really was.

08:18.493 --> 08:20.834
[SPEAKER_00]: Not a man of value, but a man of vanity.

08:24.997 --> 08:34.923
[SPEAKER_01]: To be honest with you, my keeping in you at arm's length all these years had nothing to do with your deformity.

08:36.790 --> 08:40.252
[SPEAKER_01]: It had to do with knowing this secret.

08:40.992 --> 08:48.135
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether or not Grayson was your father or forbid it, Archibald Fryholm was your father.

08:52.537 --> 09:01.961
[SPEAKER_01]: I have watched you over the years and I think you as aloof, I think you as

09:07.948 --> 09:11.671
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, socially inept in some cases.

09:12.751 --> 09:14.993
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I don't see you as a cruel man.

09:15.453 --> 09:16.954
[SPEAKER_01]: Archibald was that cruel.

09:18.135 --> 09:23.499
[SPEAKER_01]: And I don't know if it was your deformities that saved you from being able to develop his character, manipulate people,

09:35.340 --> 09:37.461
[SPEAKER_01]: It is good though that I know now that it is Grayson.

09:38.522 --> 09:42.244
[SPEAKER_01]: This takes away many concerns from me.

09:46.066 --> 09:46.586
[SPEAKER_01]: Good to know?

09:48.748 --> 09:53.591
[SPEAKER_01]: It's also good to know that your mother favored Grayson over Archibald.

09:55.251 --> 10:01.055
[SPEAKER_01]: And the fact that she would never tell me was torture beyond belief.

10:07.706 --> 10:07.966
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

10:13.068 --> 10:15.789
[SPEAKER_00]: As you read the letters, you'll know that there's a man named Zafar.

10:17.209 --> 10:19.230
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I know Zafar Azane very well.

10:21.471 --> 10:22.912
[SPEAKER_00]: I was speaking with Lady Jamis.

10:23.972 --> 10:27.293
[SPEAKER_00]: I have asked her if I could meet him.

10:29.614 --> 10:31.975
[SPEAKER_00]: She said that she would ask, but it's not guaranteed.

10:32.495 --> 10:34.476
[SPEAKER_00]: Why would you wish to meet Zafar Azane?

10:35.533 --> 10:41.538
[SPEAKER_00]: Because I have questions to ask him about what happened to my father.

10:48.083 --> 10:49.484
[SPEAKER_01]: He plays with the letters a little.

10:50.245 --> 10:54.048
[SPEAKER_01]: You can tell that he's conflicted.

10:56.790 --> 10:59.532
[SPEAKER_00]: I might need to travel to see him.

11:00.733 --> 11:01.334
[SPEAKER_00]: Travel where?

11:03.323 --> 11:04.564
[SPEAKER_00]: Where do I need to go again?

11:04.584 --> 11:05.064
[SPEAKER_00]: The key?

11:05.505 --> 11:07.747
[SPEAKER_00]: Gradsul is where he is, supposedly.

11:08.687 --> 11:10.369
[SPEAKER_00]: Gradsul is where he is, supposedly.

11:11.149 --> 11:14.812
[SPEAKER_01]: You know we are in conflict with the Duke of Rolla right now.

11:14.953 --> 11:23.119
[SPEAKER_01]: The Duke of Gradsul and the Rolla family are currently blockading our fleet and the trade routes that come to Monmurg.

11:23.480 --> 11:24.060
[SPEAKER_01]: I do know that.

11:24.761 --> 11:25.421
[SPEAKER_01]: I know very well.

11:25.541 --> 11:29.464
[SPEAKER_00]: This would be very dangerous for you to go there as a member of the royal house.

11:30.105 --> 11:31.086
[SPEAKER_00]: I know what I'm getting into.

11:32.030 --> 11:34.571
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I don't think you do know what you're getting into.

11:34.591 --> 11:35.731
[SPEAKER_01]: I know what I'm asking for.

11:36.391 --> 11:40.813
[SPEAKER_01]: You may know what you're asking for, but truthfully, you do not know what you're getting into.

11:43.593 --> 11:50.995
[SPEAKER_01]: Zvar Huzain is probably one of the most powerful wizards in the Flaness at this time.

11:51.976 --> 11:56.017
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's not clear to me just whose side he is on.

11:57.177 --> 11:59.358
[SPEAKER_01]: He has come to us for diplomatic

12:00.687 --> 12:04.150
[SPEAKER_01]: Negotiations between me and the Duke of Gradsul.

12:04.230 --> 12:07.012
[SPEAKER_01]: However, not much has been brought.

12:09.955 --> 12:14.098
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not afraid that Zafar necessarily would betray us.

12:14.799 --> 12:21.504
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I see the Duke of Rola using you as a pawn in this game that we're playing.

12:21.825 --> 12:27.710
[SPEAKER_01]: I have no doubt that he would capture you and hold you to gain some leverage on me.

12:31.302 --> 12:33.664
[SPEAKER_01]: I think it is impossible for you to go to Gradsul.

12:34.605 --> 12:35.866
[SPEAKER_01]: I doubt that he'd catch me.

12:37.807 --> 12:40.309
[SPEAKER_01]: You doubt that the Duke of Gradsul would catch you?

12:41.130 --> 12:43.111
[SPEAKER_00]: You guys barely know where I am half the time.

12:45.453 --> 12:47.414
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, well, we don't look that often.

12:47.634 --> 12:48.495
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the truth.

12:50.056 --> 12:58.623
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, the principalities, we have a good spy network, and Jamis has done a good job.

12:59.885 --> 13:00.886
[SPEAKER_01]: Casting his net.

13:03.047 --> 13:06.369
[SPEAKER_01]: They all know you, though, Paul, and they know to leave you alone.

13:09.251 --> 13:16.495
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't think the Duke of Gradsul doesn't have anything as professional as what we have, especially in Gradsul itself.

13:22.259 --> 13:22.539
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

13:24.460 --> 13:26.621
[SPEAKER_01]: No, Paul, it is too dangerous.

13:27.602 --> 13:29.343
[SPEAKER_01]: What else did Lady Azane tell you, though?

13:30.672 --> 13:33.913
[SPEAKER_01]: Did she say she would go and send messages?

13:34.634 --> 13:35.134
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, wait a second.

13:35.154 --> 13:35.994
[SPEAKER_01]: Did we talk about it?

13:36.014 --> 13:38.755
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you even mention Lady Azane?

13:38.895 --> 13:39.456
[SPEAKER_01]: Lady Jamis?

13:39.476 --> 13:40.196
[SPEAKER_01]: You didn't, did you?

13:40.436 --> 13:41.756
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't mention Lady Jamis.

13:42.117 --> 13:42.557
[SPEAKER_00]: You did?

13:42.817 --> 13:43.557
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't mention it.

13:43.617 --> 13:44.518
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

13:44.578 --> 13:46.538
[SPEAKER_01]: What else has Lady Jamis told you?

13:51.861 --> 13:53.781
[SPEAKER_01]: Did she say she would contact her brother?

13:54.582 --> 13:55.102
[SPEAKER_01]: She would try.

13:58.083 --> 13:59.364
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you be patient?

14:00.144 --> 14:00.344
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

14:00.828 --> 14:01.168
[SPEAKER_00]: For me?

14:02.169 --> 14:02.489
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

14:05.051 --> 14:08.073
[SPEAKER_01]: I think you will have that conversation with Zafar Zayn.

14:08.453 --> 14:12.416
[SPEAKER_01]: He is the ambassador to the Sea Principalities.

14:14.157 --> 14:21.042
[SPEAKER_01]: And I'll take it upon myself to send a message, a letter,

14:22.637 --> 14:27.801
[SPEAKER_01]: To the Duke of Rola asking for diplomatic relations at this time.

14:28.102 --> 14:32.545
[SPEAKER_01]: It is no doubt to me that a Zayn, Zafar Zayn, will come himself.

14:33.606 --> 14:35.288
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll leave it to Lady Jamis.

14:39.211 --> 14:40.712
[SPEAKER_01]: To get you an audience with her.

14:42.273 --> 14:43.094
[SPEAKER_01]: Would that suffice?

14:45.756 --> 14:45.997
[SPEAKER_01]: Well.

14:48.599 --> 14:48.819
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

14:49.620 --> 14:49.860
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

14:53.670 --> 14:56.892
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, to other matters.

15:07.159 --> 15:07.979
[SPEAKER_01]: May I keep these?

15:11.922 --> 15:12.222
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

15:19.607 --> 15:21.188
[SPEAKER_01]: Just that of affection for your sister.

15:22.184 --> 15:25.828
[SPEAKER_01]: If you wish to keep them, I'll give them back to you.

15:29.472 --> 15:30.854
[SPEAKER_00]: Do I believe he's telling me the truth?

15:31.414 --> 15:32.215
[SPEAKER_00]: Do an insight roll.

15:36.219 --> 15:36.660
[SPEAKER_00]: No way.

15:36.820 --> 15:37.361
[SPEAKER_01]: Which roll?

15:37.381 --> 15:37.681
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a 17.

15:39.583 --> 15:40.804
[SPEAKER_01]: He's not telling you the truth.

15:41.564 --> 15:47.587
[SPEAKER_01]: And in fact, what you think is, he means to use these to go confront Jamis.

15:48.667 --> 15:51.549
[SPEAKER_01]: Something you don't really know if you want or not.

15:52.669 --> 15:54.310
[SPEAKER_00]: No, you may not keep this, Jeon.

15:57.432 --> 15:58.792
[SPEAKER_00]: I would please like to look at them more.

16:00.393 --> 16:00.833
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

16:02.754 --> 16:03.074
Thank you.

16:03.995 --> 16:06.856
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have talked to, you have showed these to others.

16:08.017 --> 16:08.177
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

16:09.273 --> 16:09.473
[SPEAKER_00]: Who?

16:09.973 --> 16:10.494
[SPEAKER_00]: Miss Janus.

16:12.615 --> 16:12.975
[SPEAKER_01]: Alright.

16:15.976 --> 16:16.377
[SPEAKER_01]: Alright.

16:22.219 --> 16:24.681
[SPEAKER_01]: I have a job for you.

16:27.702 --> 16:28.442
[SPEAKER_01]: If you would take it.

16:29.603 --> 16:30.103
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's hear it.

16:34.245 --> 16:37.267
[SPEAKER_01]: I know that you have not been in the foreign district very often.

16:42.561 --> 16:43.542
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a wild place.

16:45.583 --> 17:09.016
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I have rumors that there are agents of the Prince of Toli

17:11.595 --> 17:22.821
[SPEAKER_01]: Unofficially residing in that province.

17:25.943 --> 17:31.186
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm going to let you, I'm going to tell you something that must be kept sacred.

17:35.268 --> 17:35.748
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm all yours.

17:39.895 --> 17:43.756
[SPEAKER_01]: I believe that Prince of Toli is working against us with the Duke of Rola.

17:45.116 --> 17:46.137
[SPEAKER_01]: With the Duke of Kratzel.

17:49.698 --> 17:49.978
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

17:54.439 --> 17:55.619
[SPEAKER_01]: I want you to find out.

17:57.940 --> 18:04.562
[SPEAKER_01]: I want you to find out if there are any agents from Toli in the foreign district.

18:07.242 --> 18:07.963
[SPEAKER_00]: And do what with them?

18:09.243 --> 18:09.563
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing.

18:15.811 --> 18:22.493
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want you to kill or try to be in conflict with anyone.

18:23.614 --> 18:25.494
[SPEAKER_01]: These men are dangerous.

18:27.255 --> 18:36.038
[SPEAKER_01]: If they are who I think they are, they are Toli assassins that work for Prince Saknod themselves.

18:37.718 --> 18:39.619
[SPEAKER_01]: These men are magical assassins.

18:41.520 --> 18:45.421
[SPEAKER_01]: They know magic as only the Toli do and the Seul do.

18:46.983 --> 18:48.024
[SPEAKER_01]: Keep your distance.

18:51.325 --> 18:53.206
[SPEAKER_01]: You can recognize them as Suel.

18:56.728 --> 18:57.588
[SPEAKER_01]: Track them down.

19:00.109 --> 19:00.830
[SPEAKER_01]: Observe them.

19:03.491 --> 19:04.251
[SPEAKER_01]: See who they meet.

19:05.312 --> 19:06.392
[SPEAKER_01]: See who they talk to.

19:10.834 --> 19:11.355
[SPEAKER_00]: It will be done.

19:14.036 --> 19:15.617
[SPEAKER_01]: I have reason to believe

19:16.481 --> 19:27.584
[SPEAKER_01]: That there is somebody in our employ that has been working closely with them.

19:33.346 --> 19:40.628
[SPEAKER_01]: Do not kill anyone or only do so if absolutely necessary.

19:45.937 --> 19:46.457
[SPEAKER_00]: I understand.

19:46.717 --> 19:47.898
[SPEAKER_00]: Can you start on this tonight?

19:50.799 --> 19:53.500
[SPEAKER_00]: There's something I want to do, but I'll get on it first thing tomorrow morning.

19:55.021 --> 19:59.023
[SPEAKER_01]: When you go to the foreign district, be sure that no one knows who you are.

20:01.024 --> 20:02.605
[SPEAKER_01]: Select a cloak.

20:03.725 --> 20:04.105
[SPEAKER_01]: I understand.

20:05.326 --> 20:05.546
[SPEAKER_01]: Here.

20:09.448 --> 20:10.848
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll have something brought to your room.

20:14.210 --> 20:14.530
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

20:17.625 --> 20:18.165
[SPEAKER_01]: All right, Paul.

20:18.325 --> 20:18.765
[SPEAKER_01]: Tomorrow.

20:21.667 --> 20:23.347
[SPEAKER_01]: You said you want the rest of the day, right?

